            <span class="faq__s" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq__a" id="fa6" role="region" aria-labelledby="fq6"><div>
            <p>Phoenix and Scottsdale, plus Tempe, Mesa, Chandler and the surrounding suburbs.
            If you are not sure whether you are in range, call with your cross streets and we
            will tell you straight away.</p>
          </div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq__i">
          <button class="faq__q" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="fa7" id="fq7">
            My door is off track. Should I keep using it?
            <span class="faq__s" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq__a" id="fa7" role="region" aria-labelledby="fq7"><div>
            <p>Stop using the opener. Every cycle on a crooked door bends panels and can snap a
            cable under load, which turns a one-hour fix into a panel replacement. Unplug the
            opener, leave the door where it is, and call us.</p>
          </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

